Fixes https://github.com/link-assistant/formal-ai/issues/980

## What failed

The seven default-branch runs named in the issue were downloaded and matched to their timestamps and SHAs. Six workflows passed. CI/CD run 31186108359 exposed three actionable defects:

- `cargo fmt --all -- --check` rejected an unformatted assertion in `tests/unit/total_closure.rs`.
- the local Rust/WASM unknown-opener spec allowed live search, so its Chinese case received ranked web results instead of exercising the local fallback;
- the permission cold-start spec returned after the click appended the user message, before the worker captured the pending task. A retry hid this race.

## Fix

- format the rejected Rust statement;
- make the opener parity spec hermetic with a browser-level cross-origin request boundary;
- wait for a worker answer and the observable `data-has-pending-task=true` state instead of an incidental message count;
- add issue-specific regression gates, requirements traceability, and a changelog fragment.

The complete issue/PR/comment/run evidence, timeline, root-cause analysis, validation logs, Hive Mind guide, and full Rust/JS/Python template snapshots are preserved in [`dev/log/issues/980/pulls/981`](https://github.com/link-assistant/formal-ai/tree/issue-980-7930e3c647c0/dev/log/issues/980/pulls/981). The audit found no new template-owned defect: the applicable template controls were already adopted in PRs 809 and 971, and PR 971 already filed the remaining upstream gaps, so this PR avoids duplicate reports.

## Reproduction and verification

- regression gates were run before the fixes and failed on the formatting/isolation invariants;
- `cargo fmt --all -- --check`;
- `cargo clippy --lib --bins --tests --all-features -- -D warnings`;
- `cargo check --examples --all-features`;
- `cargo test --all-features` — full suite green (2,597 unit tests plus integration/standalone suites; three intentionally ignored tests);
- `rust-script scripts/check-file-size.rs`;
- `rust-script scripts/check-hardcoded-language.rs`;
- `bash scripts/check-secrets.sh`;
- `npm --prefix tests/e2e run check:web-tdz`;
- `npm --prefix tests/e2e run check:web-hardcoded-ui`;
- opener parity: 12/12 across three repetitions;
- permission cold start: 9/9 across three repetitions.
